// PutTopics streams a batch of topic writes - optionally preceded by a
// web creation, and optionally interleaved with attachment uploads -
// committed as a single, all-or-nothing transaction: if any message in
// the batch fails (including the web creation, if present), nothing in
// the batch is saved, not even earlier topics/attachments that would
// have individually succeeded.
//
// create_web, if sent at all, must be the first message. An "attachment"
// message carries exactly what a standalone PutAttachment call would:
// one "metadata" message begins an upload, followed by zero or more
// "chunk" messages carrying its bytes in order; an upload ends either at
// the next non-chunk message (another attachment's metadata, a "topic",
// or end of stream) or, if this is the batch's very last message, at the
// end of the stream - same as PutAttachment's own doc comment. A batch's
// topics/attachments need not all target the same web, but any web they
// reference must already exist by the time that message is processed -
